        <item>
            <title>0.27.16</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:12:54 -0600</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>77</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.27.16</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:0;padding:2px 4px}h3{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 4px}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}}</style><h3>What's new in Keeploop 0.27.16</h3><ul><li>Agents can acknowledge route matches one by one with the new ack_hits tool. check_route with unacked_older_than_s hands back any match that was read or pushed but never acknowledged, so a session that crashes or compacts mid-task no longer loses one, and a replay no longer repeats what was already handled. check_route answers as before for agents that do not use acks.</li><li>awaiting_reply now covers texts and Slack too: source="messages" lists text conversations whose latest message is from someone else (or from you, with direction="them"), with one person's iMessage and SMS chats counted as one and short codes left out; source="slack" does the same for Slack DMs, group DMs and threads that mention you; source="all" covers every source that is on.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
